## Obsidian Pattern — Boxes and Bags

Every Obsidian block requires Boxes and Bags. Each is its own file. No exceptions.

### Bag — Server to Client Data Contract
```csharp
// [BlockName]Bag.cs
namespace org.minsol.[PluginName].ViewModels.Blocks.[BlockName]
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Data bag for the [BlockName] block entity data.
    /// </summary>
    public class [BlockName]Bag
    {
        /// <summary>Gets or sets the encrypted identifier key.</summary>
        public string IdKey { get; set; }

        /// <summary>Gets or sets [property description].</summary>
        public string SomeProperty { get; set; }
    }
}
```

### OptionsBag — Config, Dropdowns, and Reference Data
```csharp
// [BlockName]OptionsBag.cs
using Rock.ViewModels.Utility;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace org.minsol.[PluginName].ViewModels.Blocks.[BlockName]
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Options bag for the [BlockName] block containing select lists and config.
    /// </summary>
    public class [BlockName]OptionsBag
    {
        /// <summary>Gets or sets the available [entity] options.</summary>
        public List<ListItemBag> [Entity]Options { get; set; }
    }
}
```

### SaveRequestBag — Client to Server on Save
```csharp
// [BlockName]SaveRequestBag.cs
namespace org.minsol.[PluginName].ViewModels.Blocks.[BlockName]
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Save request bag containing data submitted from the [BlockName] block.
    /// </summary>
    public class [BlockName]SaveRequestBag
    {
        /// <summary>Gets or sets the encrypted identifier key.</summary>
        public string IdKey { get; set; }

        /// <summary>Gets or sets [property description].</summary>
        public string SomeProperty { get; set; }
    }
}
```

### Box — Wraps All Bags for Transport
```csharp
// [BlockName]Box.cs
using Rock.ViewModels.Blocks;

namespace org.minsol.[PluginName].ViewModels.Blocks.[BlockName]
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Initialization box for the [BlockName] block.
    /// </summary>
    public class [BlockName]Box : BlockBox
    {
        /// <summary>Gets or sets the entity bag.</summary>
        public [BlockName]Bag Entity { get; set; }

        /// <summary>Gets or sets the options bag.</summary>
        public [BlockName]OptionsBag Options { get; set; }
    }
}
```

### Multiple Bags Rule
Most blocks need more than one bag. Common set:
- `[BlockName]Bag`            → primary entity data
- `[BlockName]OptionsBag`     → select lists and configuration
- `[BlockName]SaveRequestBag` → payload sent back to server on save

Each bag is always its own `.cs` file. Never combine bags into one file.

