## TypeScript / Vue / Obsidian Patterns

### Generated ViewModels — The Type System

Running `npm run viewmodels` generates the following files from the compiled
C# DLL. These are the authoritative types for the entire frontend. Do NOT
create a `types.ts` file — it does not exist in this pattern.

```
src/
├── Core/                         ← hand-written block code lives here
├── ViewModels/                   ← AUTO-GENERATED by npm run viewmodels
│   ├── bags.d.ts                 ← all Bag types (flat, no subfolders)
│   └── boxes.d.ts                ← all Box types (flat, no subfolders)
├── enums.partial.ts              ← AUTO-GENERATED, lives in src/ root
├── shims-obs.d.ts
└── tsconfig.json
```

#### Rules for Generated ViewModels Files
- NEVER manually create or modify `bags.d.ts`, `boxes.d.ts`, or
  `enums.partial.ts` — they are always overwritten by `npm run viewmodels`.
- NEVER commit manual changes to generated files.
- ALWAYS re-run `npm run viewmodels` after any C# Bag, Box, or Enum changes.
- Import types directly from the generated files in `.obs` components.

#### Import Patterns
```typescript
// Importing a box — ViewModels/ is flat, no subfolders
import type { [BlockName]InitializationBox } from "./ViewModels/boxes";

// Importing bags — ViewModels/ is flat, no subfolders
import type { [BlockName]Bag, [BlockName]OptionsBag } from "./ViewModels/bags";

// Importing enums — lives in src/ root, NOT inside ViewModels/
import { [EnumName], [EnumName]Description } from "./enums.partial";
```

#### What The Generated Files Contain
- `boxes.d.ts` — the initialization box type passed to `useConfigurationValues`
- `bags.d.ts` — all bag types including entity, options, and save request bags
- `enums.partial.ts` — enums as `const` objects with a matching description
  `Record<number, string>` for display labels

#### Generated Enum Pattern
```typescript
// Auto-generated — do not modify
export const ProgressBarStyle = {
    Numeric: 0,
    Dots: 1,
    Bar: 2,
    Steps: 3,
    Segments: 4
} as const;

export const ProgressBarStyleDescription: Record<number, string> = {
    0: "Numeric",
    1: "Dots",
    2: "Bar",
    3: "Steps",
    4: "Segments"
};

export type ProgressBarStyle = typeof ProgressBarStyle[keyof typeof ProgressBarStyle];
```

Use the enum constant for values and the Description record for display labels:
```typescript
// Value comparison
if ( style === ProgressBarStyle.Bar ) { ... }

// Display label
const label = ProgressBarStyleDescription[style];
```

---

### utils.ts — All Shared Logic Lives Here
```typescript
// utils.ts
// Shared helper functions for the [BlockName] block.
// If a function is used in more than one place, it lives here.

import type { [BlockName]Bag } from "./ViewModels/bags";

/**
 * [Description of what this function does.]
 * @param value - [Description of parameter]
 * @returns [Description of return value]
 */
export const formatSomeValue = (value: string): string => {
    return value.trim();
};

/**
 * Validates the [BlockName] entity bag.
 * @param bag - The entity bag to validate
 * @returns Array of validation error messages, empty if valid
 */
export const validate[BlockName] = (bag: [BlockName]Bag): string[] => {
    const errors: string[] = [];

    if ( !bag.someProperty ) {
        errors.push( "Some Property is required." );
    }

    return errors;
};
```

### Root Component (.obs) — Orchestrates Only
```typescript
// [blockName].obs
// Root component. Orchestrates child components and state.
// No business logic here — delegate to computed properties and utils.ts.

<template>
    <div>
        <[SubComponent]
            v-model="entityBag"
            :options="optionsBag"
            @save="onSave" />
    </div>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
    import { ref, computed } from "vue";
    import { useConfigurationValues, useInvokeBlockAction } from "@Obsidian/Utility/block";
    import [SubComponent] from "./[SubComponent].obs";
    import { validate[BlockName] } from "./utils";
    import type { [BlockName]Bag, [BlockName]OptionsBag, [BlockName]SaveRequestBag } from "./ViewModels/bags";
    import type { [BlockName]InitializationBox } from "./ViewModels/boxes";

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Configuration and Initialization
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    const config = useConfigurationValues<[BlockName]InitializationBox>();

    const invokeBlockAction = useInvokeBlockAction();

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // State
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    const entityBag = ref<[BlockName]Bag>( config.configuration ?? {} as [BlockName]Bag );
    const isLoading = ref<boolean>( false );

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Computed
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    const validationErrors = computed((): string[] => {
        return validate[BlockName]( entityBag.value );
    });

    const isValid = computed((): boolean => {
        return validationErrors.value.length === 0;
    });

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Event Handlers
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    const onSave = async (): Promise<void> => {
        if ( !isValid.value ) {
            return;
        }

        isLoading.value = true;

        try {
            const request: [BlockName]SaveRequestBag = {
                idKey: entityBag.value.idKey,
                someProperty: entityBag.value.someProperty
            };

            await invokeBlockAction( "Save", { request } );
        }
        finally {
            isLoading.value = false;
        }
    };
</script>
```

### Template Rules
```
✅ Templates are declarative markup only
✅ Use computed properties for all derived values
✅ Use named event handlers for all interactions
✅ v-if / v-for only reference computed properties or state refs

❌ No method calls with logic inside template expressions
❌ No .filter(), .map(), .reduce() directly in the template
❌ No ternary expressions longer than a simple null check
❌ No business logic of any kind inside <template>
```

---

## Canonical File Templates
# Create every file below from scratch. Never copy from an existing plugin.
# Replace [PluginName] with PascalCase and [pluginname] with lowercase.

### org.minsol.[PluginName].sln
Location: `[PluginName]/org.minsol.[PluginName].sln`

Every plugin has its own `.sln` file containing only the C# project.
This is completely independent of `Rock.sln` — never add plugin projects
to `Rock.sln`. The Obsidian frontend project is NOT included in the `.sln`
since it is built independently via `npm run build`.

Generate a new GUID for the plugin project using PowerShell:
```bash
powershell.exe -Command "[System.Guid]::NewGuid().ToString().ToUpper()"
```

```
Microsoft Visual Studio Solution File, Format Version 12.00
# Visual Studio Version 17
VisualStudioVersion = 17.5.2.0
MinimumVisualStudioVersion = 10.0.40219.1
Project("{FAE04EC0-301F-11D3-BF4B-00C04F79EFBC}") = "org.minsol.[PluginName]", "org.minsol.[PluginName]\org.minsol.[PluginName].csproj", "{YOUR-NEW-GUID}"
EndProject
Global
	GlobalSection(SolutionConfigurationPlatforms) = preSolution
		Debug|Any CPU = Debug|Any CPU
		Release|Any CPU = Release|Any CPU
	EndGlobalSection
	GlobalSection(ProjectConfigurationPlatforms) = postSolution
		{YOUR-NEW-GUID}.Debug|Any CPU.ActiveCfg = Debug|Any CPU
		{YOUR-NEW-GUID}.Debug|Any CPU.Build.0 = Debug|Any CPU
		{YOUR-NEW-GUID}.Release|Any CPU.ActiveCfg = Release|Any CPU
		{YOUR-NEW-GUID}.Release|Any CPU.Build.0 = Release|Any CPU
	EndGlobalSection
	GlobalSection(SolutionProperties) = preSolution
		HideSolutionNode = FALSE
	EndGlobalSection
	GlobalSection(ExtensibilityGlobals) = postSolution
		SolutionGuid = {YOUR-SECOND-NEW-GUID}
	EndGlobalSection
EndGlobal
```

Replace `{YOUR-NEW-GUID}` with the generated GUID (appears 5 times).
Replace `{YOUR-SECOND-NEW-GUID}` with a second newly generated GUID
for the SolutionGuid — these must be different from each other.

